# Camouflage replaces the declaration of blockers itself (CR 614.1a), whoever would have made it, and its own words say
# who makes its choices: "each defending player chooses any number of creatures they control and divides them into ...
# piles". So with Melee also cast, Bot2 - not Melee's caster - makes the pile, and Phyrexian Walker in it blocks Memnite,
# the only attacker (CR 509.1). No ruling covers the pair; this is the reading of the two texts with the CR.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Memnite
Camouflage
Melee
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Melee.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Phyrexian Walker)
? Combat.Blocks = Phyrexian Walker > Memnite
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.Damage = 1
